# CHANGELOG.md is generated by git-cliff (see .github/workflows/changelog.yml), never
# edited by hand. Two branches therefore hold two independently generated copies, and a
# textual three-way merge of them produces a scrambled file — sections out of order,
# entries duplicated — which then gets committed and has to be untangled by a person.
#
# `union` keeps both sides' lines instead of conflicting. The result can contain duplicate
# entries for a moment; the next tag push regenerates the whole file on main and normalises
# it. A transient duplicate is a far smaller cost than a blocked PR plus a hand-merge of a
# machine-written file.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
